<title>CANADA: Whirlpool files suit against Maytag.</title>
<headline>Whirlpool files suit against Maytag.</headline>
<dateline>MISSISSAUGA 1996-09-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Whirlpool Corp and its wholly owned Canadian unit Inglis Ltd said on Tuesday that they filed a lawsuit with the Federal Court of Canada against Maytag Corp, Canadian unit Maytag Ltd and Canadian distributor Maytag Quebec Inc.</p>
<p>They said in a statement that &quot;...certain automatic washer models built by Maytag and marketed and distributed by its affiliates violate a Canadian patent held by Whirlpool.&quot; &quot;...several models of a Maytag washer recently introduced in Canada infringe a Canadian patent issued in 1981 covering Whirlpool's unique two-way agitator,&quot; they said.</p>
</text>
